8 questions, 3 runs each — 24 answers

  first answer     figure 24/24   cause 21/24    2,091 tokens/answer
  after a critic   figure 24/24   cause 21/24    3,930 tokens/answer

  accuracy 94% -> 94%   for 1.9x the tokens
  the critic found something to say 12 times, and passed 12

It changed nothing at all, for 1.9x the tokens.

The critic objected 12 times out of 24 and passed the other 12. Every one of
those objections cost a second full answer, and on this task set they did not
buy a better one.

That is consistent with §9.6, where self-reflection was the worst of four
prompting patterns, and the reason is the same. The mistakes here are not
visible in the output: a cause that is subtly the wrong quarter reads
perfectly well. Checking it means searching the documents again, which is not
reviewing — it is redoing the work and hoping the second attempt is luckier.
